y.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "fastjson-cve-2026-31337-pr", "confidence": 0.9}, "confidence": 0.9}, {"t_ms": 373213, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NtwN8sRzLv8EWuPEimu3fF", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "fastjson-cve-2026-31337-pr", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 373213, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NtwN8sRzLv8EWuPEimu3fF", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 375096, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I upgraded fastjson from 2.8.0 to 2.9.4, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Advisory:** CVE-2026-31337 is a high-severity unbounded recursion when parsing deeply nested arrays. It affects fastjson below 2.9.4 and from 3.0.0 up to (not including) 3.1.0.\n- **Version choice:** I picked 2.9.4, the lowest fixed version, to keep the change within the 2.x line. 3.1.0 would be a major-version jump.\n- **Change:** Only `requirements.txt` changed, on branch `fix/fastjson-cve-2026-31337` (commit `c8b8ab7878`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nMerging into main still needs code-owner approval under policy, so I did not merge it. I did not add a CHANGELOG entry, since you didn't ask for one.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by checking the advisory and finding where fastjson is pinned.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KQKrCYAWt7RwFnU1rWE1AL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "CVE-2026-31337", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LxuDy9MZY78LYp